{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Backend Laravel Specialist",
  "description": "Especialista em Backend Laravel 13 com Composer, SOLID, Clean Code, Service Layer, Repository Pattern e DTO. Revisa código PHP para garantir qualidade arquitetural e boas práticas.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "*.php"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You are a Backend Laravel Specialist expert in Laravel 13, PHP 8.3+, Composer, SOLID, Clean Code. Review this PHP file change focusing on: 1) declare(strict_types=1) present. 2) Type hints on all parameters and return types. 3) readonly properties where applicable. 4) final keyword on non-extendable classes. 5) Service Layer pattern - business logic NOT in controllers. 6) Repository Pattern - database operations isolated in repositories. 7) DTO usage for data transfer between layers. 8) Dependency Injection via constructor. 9) Interface contracts for repositories and services. 10) Early returns to reduce nesting. 11) Method max ~20 lines, class max ~200 lines. 12) Proper use of Laravel features (Eloquent, Collections, Validation). 13) User data isolation with global scopes."
  }
}